WEBVTT

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:22.060
<i>The Last Days of the Tokugawa Shogunate</i>

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:28.020
<i>Kyoto</i>

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:49.760
<i>During the Bakumatsu,</i>
<i>there was a man called the Hitokiri Battosai.</i>

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:53.060
<i>He was feared by all.</i>

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:10.950
<i>Rurouni Kenshin The Movie</i>
<i>- Requiem for Restoration Patriots -</i>

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:17.000
<i>Meiji 11</i>

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:24.050
<i>Yokohama</i>

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:07.610
Western architecture and gas lamps?

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:09.320
Get out of the way!

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.610
Oh, I'm terribly sorry.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:13.160
No problem. No problem.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:16.660
Just watch where you're going
from now on, samurai boy.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:19.080
Boy?

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:22.500
Kenshin, this way!

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:26.540
You're going to get lost
if you don't watch out.

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:28.960
Don't get mad at him, Yahiko.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:31.510
Kenshin's just happy
he got to ride the locomotive.

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.890
It's as incredible as I thought it would be.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:45.310
Why do we do this?

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:48.900
Traveling all the way to Yokohama
just to look at stupid buildings.

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:50.900
And on top of that
we had to travel by locomotive.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:53.490
You're the one who
was the most excited about the train.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:57.870
If you feel that way,
you can pay me back for the train tickets!

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:01.080
Yeah, well, anyway,

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:04.710
don't you think all of
these buildings look the same?

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:07.750
Yes, I guess so.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:12.050
Japan is changing,

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.180
and that's good.

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:25.060
Pretty impressive, wasn't it?

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:27.440
What the hell are you talking about?
That's just brute strength.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:28.940
What did you say?

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:34.400
We're not monkeys. We can use tools.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:39.240
Don't go over there. It's dangerous.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:43.080
Stop that right now!
You're making trouble for everyone!

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:50.420
We came to this country
to create a little goodwill, but mostly...

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:53.050
we just want to get friendly
with some of the ladies.

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:57.130
Hey, cutie. Nippon, Shogun,
Mount Fuji, Geisha.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:58.890
You wanna get it on?

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:00.430
Please don't.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.430
Let's have some fun.

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:06.480
Let's get to know each other
a little better, baby.

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:07.730
Let me go!

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:10.440
- Do something about this.
- Why don't you?

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:12.280
No!

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:17.950
Stop this nonsense right now
or you will get hurt.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:20.070
- What's going on?
- Who the hell are you?

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:24.790
This bastard wants to ruin our party.

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:28.250
Toki, stand back.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:29.500
Yes.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.670
Hey, don't go away mad!

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:37.880
Just joking! Just joking!

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:40.340
You'll understand it
after I explain it to you.

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.180
If I explain it!

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:46.140
Did he use his sword?

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:47.940
I don't know. It happened so fast!

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:50.650
He's good.

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:56.950
That's what you get!

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.990
Bastard! Hey, guys,
let's take his head off!

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:08.830
He's a powerful man.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:11.000
Yahiko, give me your bamboo sword!

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:12.460
I want to help that man.

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:14.840
He won't need it.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:20.550
If you think our customs do not apply to you
because you are foreigners, you are wrong.

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:23.680
Here!

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.430
Anyone ever tell you
that you talk too much?

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:36.570
- Bastard!
- Big mouth!

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.330
Hey, up here!

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:48.870
Bring your weapons and come up here!

00:09:57.920 --> 00:09:59.720
Look out! More foreigners!

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:05.850
Watch out!

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:13.060
You shouldn't use firearms
in a fight like this.

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.570
Kenshin, where's Kenshin?

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:25.200
Kenshin, did you cut him?

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:27.240
Of course not.

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:33.460
You know I can't slash anyone
with this sword.

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:35.000
Oh, right.

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:43.930
Stop it right now!

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:47.560
Kenshin, they might not like to see
a guy with a sword around here.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:48.850
You better run.

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:51.930
Hey, Samurai, you better get out of here!

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:55.230
Toki, best if you hide too.
We will meet later.

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:58.610
- Let's go.
- Here, this way.

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:01.400
We're not done with you, bastard!

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:04.740
And I'm not done with you!

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:10.240
What's going on over there?

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:13.790
Noisy rats, why can't they
let us have a little more fun?

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:18.880
Well, what shall I do now?

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:21.880
I guess I'm caught between
the devil and the deep blue sea.

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:25.300
All right, I'll finish you off.
Come on, big boy!

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:26.970
Son of a bitch!

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:30.560
What the hell is this?

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:32.020
It's not my fault!

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:33.480
Shut up, you!

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:34.810
You wanna fight?

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:39.650
Have fun!

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:52.620
Is your friend going to be all right?

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:56.290
Sure, you don't have to worry
about Sanosuke at all.

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:59.210
You did a good job out there.

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:01.260
No, I didn't do anything.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:02.880
You are too modest.

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:05.300
So, why do you carry
a sword with a reverse edge?

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:08.600
You recognized it.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:13.480
Years ago, I swore
I would never kill anyone, ever again.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:14.810
I see.

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:18.610
The use of violence makes you sick
when you think about it.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.870
Those who died during the Bakumatsu

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.500
don't have to see how
the Meiji government is rotten to the core.

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:42.130
If they could see it,
they would shed tears of anguish.

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:46.300
No, maybe they would laugh at the irony.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:51.680
The sky I saw then was so blue.

00:12:55.270 --> 00:12:58.940
The sky must be high and clear, right?

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:00.400
Yes.

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:03.860
Well, I cannot leave Toki alone.

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:05.030
May I have your name?

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:07.410
Kenshin, my name is Kenshin Himura.

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:10.370
I am Takimi Shigure.

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:12.830
Takimi Shigure?

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:14.960
I hope we meet again.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:16.920
I would like that.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:30.010
What do you want?

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:35.180
You're as gruff as always.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:37.850
Look who's talking.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:41.190
You didn't come to Yokohama
to see the sights, did you?

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:44.110
Let me give you some advice.

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:47.200
Stay away from that man.

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:51.910
Takimi Shigure,
he's a very dangerous man.

00:13:57.910 --> 00:14:01.790
She's a beautiful woman, isn't she?
She's so different from someone.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.420
Who do you mean by "someone"?

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:06.670
Hey, did you happen to get her name?

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:08.050
- Of course.
- Good!

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:09.720
Geez, you are both idiots!

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:12.390
The daughter of a Samurai from what
was the Aizu clan, her name's Toki.

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:14.100
Miss Toki Takatsuki!

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:18.060
Did you say the Aizu clan?
I bet she's had a rough life.

00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:20.480
I don't think
that means the same thing to me.

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:21.520
<i>Aizu!</i>

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:23.610
What are you talking about?
I just mean she's had a tough life.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:26.480
No, I think you mean she's had a hard life
because she's so pretty.

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:28.740
Yeah, maybe so.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:33.830
<i>Takatsuki of the Aizu Clan...</i>

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:54.180
You fools!

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:55.760
Boy, am I starving!

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:58.310
Okay! Yokohama is a city of foreigners,

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.100
and foreigners eat beef.

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:01.350
What kind of logic is that?

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:04.650
It's the reason Sanosuke came to Yokohama
with us, isn't it?

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:06.190
Damn right.

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:10.280
I see. But unlike the Akabeko,
it's harder to scam free meals here.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:14.240
Let's see.
What am I going to do with you?

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:17.580
Don't take it that way.
I'll pay you back when we get home.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:18.950
Come on, Yahiko,
why don't you ask her, too!

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:21.370
Hey, I'm staying out of this.

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:22.960
Shut up!

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:34.970
Attack!

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:56.030
- Kenshin!
- Got it.

00:15:58.830 --> 00:15:59.830
What's the matter?

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:00.830
Are they dead?

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:02.830
No, I think they're just unconscious.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.210
Out of the way!

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:13.090
Whoa! Whoa!

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:15.550
Baron Tamono!

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:17.180
Kawai, report this
to headquarters on the double.

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:18.180
Yes, Sir.

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:19.680
Sakashita, report
to the nearest police station.

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:21.020
Yes, Sir.

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:22.730
First Troop, move forward.

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:25.560
Advance now,
but do not fire until I give the command.

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:26.690
Go!

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:31.150
- Second Troop, circle the perimeter.
- Yes, Sir.

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:33.950
All others, guard this place
and protect the civilians.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:35.030
Yes, Sir.

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:38.030
It is very dangerous here.
Please stand back.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:41.870
He's cool!

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:44.410
Form a double line!

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:48.500
Perfect! Withdraw according to our plan.

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:55.380
Do not let them escape! Pursue them!

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:05.270
After them! Do not let them get away!

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:22.080
Well, we certainly saw
a lot of things today, didn't we?

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:24.950
Yokohama's a pretty exciting place.

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:26.080
Let's see...

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:30.250
A steam train, Toki Takatsuki,
and I paid for your beef meal.

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:33.300
That soldier was really amazing.

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:36.800
Huh?
Do you want to be a soldier too?

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:41.260
No, I don't want to join the military.
You see... How can I explain this?

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:43.100
Either way, you'd have to learn
to ride a horse first.

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:44.100
I will!

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:48.730
But I hear each horse judges its rider.
I hope you don't fall off.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:50.270
Right, Kenshin?

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:52.110
- Damn right.
- Shut up.

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:01.450
Let's go home.

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:04.200
Sure, I guess so.

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:16.210
<i>Tokyo</i>

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:20.260
Thank you, teacher!

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:21.390
Thank you!

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:23.470
Goodbye! Hey, hurry up!

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:26.430
Wait for me!

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:30.270
Goodbye, be careful.

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:32.310
Yes, Ma'am!

00:19:03.340 --> 00:19:05.310
Are the children gone?

00:19:05.430 --> 00:19:06.600
Yes.

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:12.850
Gentatsu has been gone
for fourteen years, hasn't he?

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:16.690
Yes, he died when I was four years old.

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:20.490
I have been living here ever since.

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:23.570
Time has gone by so quickly.

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:28.330
What were you thinking about earlier?
You looked scary.

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:30.500
Oh, it was nothing.

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:33.290
Hey, Shigure, are you home?

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:34.330
There you are.

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:35.670
Kajiki...

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:53.060
What is the matter?

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:56.360
Shigure, all went according to your plan.

00:19:56.480 --> 00:20:00.440
The state guest from England was supposed to
go to Kyoto from Yokohama,

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:03.110
But he changed his plan instead to
come to Tokyo in six days.

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:06.620
I have also arranged for another cannon.

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:08.450
That is encouraging.

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:11.960
Shigure, I want you to
take command of the final assault.

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:14.120
Yes, I understand.

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:18.590
We cannot turn back now,
for Gentatsu's sake.

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:23.260
I will never forget that night.

00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:30.470
It's me.

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:38.820
I heard that the Satsuma and Choshu
are making an alliance.

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:40.730
Is it true, Gentatsu?

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:42.190
Yes, I am positive.

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:45.280
They are holding
a secret meeting about it tonight.

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:48.660
They will do anything
to destroy the Tokugawa Shogunate.

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:53.750
The attendees will be Takamori Saigo
of the Satsuma and Kogoro Katsura of the Choshu.

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:57.670
Saigo and Katsura? Impressive meeting.

00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:00.960
Ryoma Sakamoto who acted as a go-between
for them will probably be there, too.

00:21:01.130 --> 00:21:03.920
All the leaders of the rebellion
in one place on one night.

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:06.970
If we can attack them,
we can alter the flow of history.

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:08.970
The Aizu clan would save face.

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:10.760
We could control the Shogunate.

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:11.810
Shigure!

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:13.140
Shigure!

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:15.480
Well, where will they meet?

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:18.350
We have narrowed it down
to three different places.

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:21.730
We considered Masudaya,
which the Satsuma use regularly.

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:25.240
But the Shinsengumi are guarding
that place, so it will not be there.

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:27.490
The most likely places are Suzuya,

00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:29.450
or the lumberyard of Minoda.

00:21:29.570 --> 00:21:30.660
Those are quite far from each other.

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:33.830
That is why
we cannot decide where to go.

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:36.870
I think Suzuya is the place.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:40.340
No, the Suzuya has
very few escape routes around it.

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:44.510
They would never choose
a dangerous location like that.

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:45.840
He is right.

00:21:46.920 --> 00:21:48.640
I have decided on Minoda.

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:51.640
We will regret it
if we miss out on this opportunity.

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:53.180
Yes!

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:56.390
Right, let's go.

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:06.400
What is wrong, Gentatsu?

00:22:07.400 --> 00:22:09.740
I cannot ignore my instincts.
I am going to Suzuya.

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:11.320
Gentatsu...

00:22:11.450 --> 00:22:12.530
It is just a strong feeling.

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:15.500
If I am wrong,
I will come immediately to join you.

00:22:17.540 --> 00:22:20.750
I understand. If that is how you feel.

00:22:21.040 --> 00:22:23.210
Sakurai, Asami, and Yokota,
take your groups with him.

00:22:23.340 --> 00:22:24.250
Yes, Sir.

00:22:24.380 --> 00:22:26.050
Thank you.

00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:10.220
Damn!

00:23:24.360 --> 00:23:25.820
Gentatsu!

00:23:35.450 --> 00:23:37.120
Gentatsu!

00:23:47.750 --> 00:23:50.300
I am so sorry, Gentatsu.

00:23:50.420 --> 00:23:52.970
It was...
It was...

00:23:53.340 --> 00:23:55.680
It was my mistake!

00:23:56.100 --> 00:23:58.970
Forgive me, Gentatsu!

00:24:10.860 --> 00:24:16.200
If we had followed Gentatsu's advice,
he would not have died.

00:24:16.780 --> 00:24:20.080
If we had smashed the alliance,

00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:24.210
the Aizu clan would not have
suffered so much tragedy.

00:24:24.330 --> 00:24:25.500
The battle of Aizu,

00:24:25.630 --> 00:24:28.210
the atrocity of the Byakkotai,
would have been avoided.

00:24:28.380 --> 00:24:32.260
All of it is my fault.

00:24:32.380 --> 00:24:35.340
All of those were caused
by my lack of judgment.

00:24:35.510 --> 00:24:38.220
I feel the guilt of that decision
every single day,

00:24:38.890 --> 00:24:41.520
every time my loved ones are in pain.

00:24:41.640 --> 00:24:44.850
But the day to avenge Gentatsu
has finally come!

00:24:45.440 --> 00:24:47.360
I cannot live peacefully,

00:24:47.520 --> 00:24:49.520
or I will have no excuse
to offer Gentatsu.

00:24:58.330 --> 00:24:59.280
I am leaving.

00:24:59.410 --> 00:25:00.290
Where are you going?

00:25:00.410 --> 00:25:02.040
You do not need to know.

00:25:02.660 --> 00:25:03.960
I will be late.

00:25:12.720 --> 00:25:14.590
<i>Kamiya Kasshin-Ryu</i>
<i>Swordsmanship Practice Hall</i>

00:25:16.140 --> 00:25:18.310
Wait! Wait!

00:25:18.470 --> 00:25:19.520
Wait!

00:25:19.640 --> 00:25:21.060
Stay inside the gate!

00:25:21.180 --> 00:25:22.100
Yes, Ma'am!

00:25:24.400 --> 00:25:25.860
Kaoru!

00:25:27.650 --> 00:25:28.650
What is it?

00:25:28.820 --> 00:25:32.110
There's a strange person
looking around outside the dojo.

00:25:32.650 --> 00:25:36.530
Really! If it's another solicitor,
I'm going to kick them right out!

00:25:46.880 --> 00:25:49.170
Oh, Miss Toki!

00:25:51.010 --> 00:25:52.010
Welcome.

00:25:52.130 --> 00:25:53.010
Welcome!

00:25:54.340 --> 00:25:55.260
Good day to you.

00:25:55.380 --> 00:25:57.140
This is our practice hall.

00:25:57.260 --> 00:26:00.350
I'll take you around to the front
where we welcome our guests.

00:26:07.480 --> 00:26:08.520
Here you are.

00:26:08.690 --> 00:26:11.030
Thank you. But please don't go to
any trouble on my account.

00:26:11.150 --> 00:26:13.070
Is Mr. Himura in?

00:26:13.190 --> 00:26:14.490
- Kenshin?
- Yes.

00:26:14.610 --> 00:26:16.530
I have something
I need to discuss with him.

00:26:16.780 --> 00:26:19.030
Oh, man.
She didn't come to see me.

00:26:19.160 --> 00:26:21.540
Kenshin always gets
the most delicious parts.

00:26:22.120 --> 00:26:24.710
Kenshin is out buying tofu.

00:26:24.830 --> 00:26:26.040
Tofu?

00:26:26.210 --> 00:26:28.000
Grocery shopping is his chore.

00:26:28.130 --> 00:26:30.880
Well, take this then.

00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:33.380
You should all have this.

00:26:33.550 --> 00:26:35.550
- Oh, my!
- That looks delicious!

00:26:35.680 --> 00:26:38.550
But it's kind of a waste
even if the fish is fresh...

00:26:38.720 --> 00:26:40.600
..when the skill of the person
who cooks it is lacking.

00:26:40.720 --> 00:26:42.810
What do you mean by that?

00:26:46.020 --> 00:26:47.270
I hate to put you to work, Miss Toki.

00:26:47.400 --> 00:26:49.940
Oh, not at all. I love to cook.

00:26:52.780 --> 00:26:54.400
It looks delicious!

00:26:54.570 --> 00:26:56.400
Please eat as much as you want.

00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:58.740
Thanks for the meal!

00:27:01.410 --> 00:27:02.620
Incredible!

00:27:02.740 --> 00:27:03.910
It is really wonderful.

00:27:04.080 --> 00:27:07.040
This is so different from the meals
we're used to eating around here.

00:27:07.920 --> 00:27:10.170
The difference is in the ingredients!

00:27:10.920 --> 00:27:13.210
Enhance the quality or kill
it depending on the skill of the cook.

00:27:13.340 --> 00:27:15.920
You two don't get to eat tomorrow!

00:27:16.050 --> 00:27:18.340
I mean, it does depend on
the quality of the ingredients.

00:27:18.470 --> 00:27:19.930
Isn't that right, Yahiko?

00:27:20.090 --> 00:27:21.720
Why can't you answer, Yahiko?

00:27:22.310 --> 00:27:24.100
It smells so good.

00:27:24.220 --> 00:27:26.270
Welcome home, Kenshin.

00:27:27.270 --> 00:27:28.770
Miss Toki...

00:27:31.110 --> 00:27:33.940
Here is the tofu, Miss Kaoru.

00:27:34.070 --> 00:27:36.030
Oh, sorry. We don't need it
for tonight's dinner anymore.

00:27:36.150 --> 00:27:37.280
What?

00:27:37.450 --> 00:27:38.780
Speaking of that, Kenshin,

00:27:38.910 --> 00:27:41.990
Miss Toki came to
speak with you about something.

00:27:51.000 --> 00:27:52.460
Well, it is that...

00:27:52.590 --> 00:27:54.170
What is it?

00:27:54.300 --> 00:27:56.130
I must speak with you about Shigure.

00:27:56.300 --> 00:27:59.180
Mr. Shigure? What is your relation?

00:27:59.510 --> 00:28:04.350
He was an ally of my late elder brother
during the Bakumatsu.

00:28:04.470 --> 00:28:05.810
Your late elder brother?

00:28:05.970 --> 00:28:09.690
Yes, he was my only family, so...

00:28:09.980 --> 00:28:12.940
Was your brother a...

00:28:13.060 --> 00:28:17.360
He was Gentatsu Takatsuki
of the Aizu clan.

00:28:17.820 --> 00:28:19.280
<i>I thought so.</i>

00:28:20.240 --> 00:28:22.320
He was one of
the three great Kanuma swordsmen?

00:28:22.490 --> 00:28:23.780
Yes.

00:28:30.410 --> 00:28:32.710
I'm astonished by the two of you.

00:28:32.830 --> 00:28:35.040
How long will you turn
your backs on each other?

00:28:35.170 --> 00:28:37.050
Mr. Katsura? Mr. Saigo?

00:28:39.970 --> 00:28:41.930
This is not good, not good.

00:28:42.050 --> 00:28:44.010
The Satsuma and Choshu clans
cannot go on like this.

00:28:44.180 --> 00:28:47.680
If they do, the dawning of a new era
will never occur in Japan.

00:28:50.690 --> 00:28:52.020
Is it the Shinsengumi?
Or the Shogunate guards?

00:28:52.190 --> 00:28:53.850
Protect Mr. Katsura and Mr. Saigo!

00:28:54.020 --> 00:28:54.860
We'll take care of them.

00:28:55.020 --> 00:28:56.400
- Understood.
- Please!

00:28:58.940 --> 00:29:01.530
Hitokiri(assassin) Gentatsu
of the Aizu clan!

00:29:01.990 --> 00:29:04.450
Where is Katsura?
Bring me Saigo and Sakamoto!

00:30:01.880 --> 00:30:05.840
Gentatsu Takatsuki of the Aizu clan,
called Hitokiri Gentatsu.

00:30:05.970 --> 00:30:10.310
One of the best Kanuma swordsmen.
He was incredible.

00:30:11.270 --> 00:30:12.640
Excuse me.

00:30:13.600 --> 00:30:14.980
Is something wrong?

00:30:15.100 --> 00:30:16.230
Nothing.

00:30:16.400 --> 00:30:21.440
Recently,
Shigure has been acting strangely.

00:30:21.570 --> 00:30:24.400
He looks very sad, and seems to be
thinking about something serious.

00:30:24.530 --> 00:30:28.950
But after we returned from Yokohama,
he spoke highly of you.

00:30:29.120 --> 00:30:30.120
Of me?

00:30:30.790 --> 00:30:33.290
He said, "I am glad to find a man
like him in times like these."

00:30:33.410 --> 00:30:36.120
And, "I have finally met
a true Samurai after all these years."

00:30:36.250 --> 00:30:39.210
I feel the same way about him.

00:30:39.340 --> 00:30:40.670
Please do me a favor.

00:30:40.800 --> 00:30:43.670
He will not open up to me.

00:30:43.800 --> 00:30:47.640
But if you spoke with him, Mr. Himura,
he would tell you something.

00:30:47.760 --> 00:30:49.390
I feel so uneasy lately!

00:30:50.390 --> 00:30:51.390
Miss Toki...

00:31:01.770 --> 00:31:05.150
I hate to put you
to the trouble of walking me home.

00:31:05.280 --> 00:31:08.820
It's no trouble.
It's my duty as a gentleman.

00:31:10.660 --> 00:31:13.830
What a mansion!

00:31:14.160 --> 00:31:16.040
Please come in.

00:31:16.500 --> 00:31:18.330
Please excuse me.

00:31:22.800 --> 00:31:24.340
You're home, Toki.

00:31:24.670 --> 00:31:25.760
Good day, Sir.

00:31:25.880 --> 00:31:29.590
Yahiko walked me home.
He lives with Mr. Himura.

00:31:29.970 --> 00:31:31.850
With Mr. Himura?

00:31:32.180 --> 00:31:33.350
Yes, Sir.

00:31:33.640 --> 00:31:35.850
You look like a fine young man.

00:31:37.520 --> 00:31:40.230
I am Yahiko Myojin of Tokyo,
child of a former samurai family!

00:31:40.350 --> 00:31:42.820
A samurai family?
Who was your father?

00:31:43.020 --> 00:31:46.070
He was a member of the Shogitai,
and died for his beliefs.

00:31:46.320 --> 00:31:50.820
The Shogitai? I'm sure he was
a greatly respected man, wasn't he?

00:31:51.160 --> 00:31:52.370
Yes, sir.

00:31:52.490 --> 00:31:55.290
Feel free to ask me
for any favor you may require.

00:31:55.410 --> 00:31:57.040
I would be glad to help you
regardless of the effort involved.

00:31:57.210 --> 00:31:58.330
Thank you very much.

00:31:59.250 --> 00:32:00.330
Mr. Shigure!

00:32:00.710 --> 00:32:03.500
Musashino, good timing.

00:32:04.460 --> 00:32:07.760
This is Yahiko, a friend of Mr. Himura,
of whom I have told you.

00:32:07.880 --> 00:32:10.300
It is a great coincidence, Musashino.

00:32:10.430 --> 00:32:14.050
Yahiko's father died
as a member of the Shogitai.

00:32:14.180 --> 00:32:15.600
I see.

00:32:15.720 --> 00:32:19.230
Musashino's father also died
while a member of the Shogitai.

00:32:20.900 --> 00:32:23.060
You have had a very hard life,
haven't you?

00:32:23.230 --> 00:32:24.400
Not really.

00:32:24.520 --> 00:32:26.070
Let us continue to do our best.

00:32:26.230 --> 00:32:27.110
Right.

00:32:27.610 --> 00:32:32.110
Yahiko, eat with us this evening.
Take a relaxing bath as well.

00:32:32.240 --> 00:32:34.330
Think of this as your home.

00:32:34.450 --> 00:32:35.370
Yes, sir!

00:32:46.460 --> 00:32:48.800
<i>Gentatsu Takatsuki...</i>

00:33:01.770 --> 00:33:05.560
You can't stop thinking about him.
Shigure, I mean.

00:33:06.270 --> 00:33:09.110
Takimi Shigure...

00:33:14.200 --> 00:33:16.740
Hey, where are you going, Yahiko?

00:33:16.870 --> 00:33:18.290
You haven't finished practice yet.

00:33:18.450 --> 00:33:21.250
I'm going to visit Mr. Shigure.

00:33:21.370 --> 00:33:22.290
Again?

00:33:22.410 --> 00:33:25.250
He has a beautiful lady at his house.

00:33:25.380 --> 00:33:26.380
Hey!

00:33:26.750 --> 00:33:28.880
Jeez, what kind of attitude is that?

00:33:30.130 --> 00:33:31.880
May I?

00:33:34.840 --> 00:33:35.970
Your waist is unprepared for attack.

00:33:36.100 --> 00:33:37.180
Yes, Sir.

00:33:40.390 --> 00:33:42.230
Ouch.

00:33:42.350 --> 00:33:43.850
What was that?

00:33:44.440 --> 00:33:45.850
I'm not finished yet!

00:33:46.310 --> 00:33:48.150
Please move the brush this way.

00:33:48.520 --> 00:33:49.690
Yes, Ma'am.

00:33:51.150 --> 00:33:53.490
Mr. Himura!

00:33:54.570 --> 00:33:56.200
Thank you for listening to me
the other day.

00:33:56.320 --> 00:33:57.530
A private school?

00:33:57.660 --> 00:34:00.370
Yes, but I am hoping to
become a better teacher.

00:34:00.490 --> 00:34:01.950
Is Mr. Shigure in?

00:34:02.080 --> 00:34:06.500
Well, he has not come home
since yesterday evening.

00:34:06.670 --> 00:34:10.170
I see. Could you give him
a message for me, then?

00:34:10.300 --> 00:34:11.670
Ask him to meet me tomorrow at six.

00:34:11.800 --> 00:34:14.220
I will be at the Ohashi Bridge
next to the shrine.

00:34:15.630 --> 00:34:18.220
Yes, I will tell him.

00:34:18.850 --> 00:34:20.010
Well, then.

00:34:20.890 --> 00:34:23.390
I am sorry he is not here.

00:34:30.320 --> 00:34:34.150
Army Minister Yamagata and
Superintendent General Kawaji,

00:34:34.280 --> 00:34:35.740
I must offer my opinion to you.

00:34:36.160 --> 00:34:38.120
You may proceed, Tamono.

00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:42.040
Yes, sir. This may not be
appropriate for me to say,

00:34:42.200 --> 00:34:45.910
but I have been thinking about the recent attack
on the British embassy in Yokohama.

00:34:46.040 --> 00:34:48.710
We should take into account
their target was the English Consulate,

00:34:48.830 --> 00:34:51.800
and we should increase the guard
along the parade route this week.

00:34:54.510 --> 00:34:56.130
This is your recommendation?

00:34:56.430 --> 00:34:58.090
There may be radical elements
thriving in Tokyo.

00:34:58.220 --> 00:35:00.050
An assault on a foreign minister would
bring shame upon Japan.

00:35:00.220 --> 00:35:02.640
I urge you to order reinforcements
for the patrol during the parade.

00:35:02.770 --> 00:35:08.150
Furthermore, I think you should take
personal command during the visit.

00:35:09.400 --> 00:35:11.610
Tamono's request is reasonable.

00:35:11.730 --> 00:35:12.650
Agreed.

00:35:12.780 --> 00:35:15.650
Tamono, you will assist me in the command
the day of the parade.

00:35:16.030 --> 00:35:17.150
Yes, sir!

00:35:23.790 --> 00:35:25.580
Hurry up! Do not be slow!

00:35:25.700 --> 00:35:28.620
We must finish the transport tonight.

00:35:29.920 --> 00:35:31.250
Kajiki, how is it going?

00:35:31.420 --> 00:35:33.090
Everything is fine.

00:35:37.800 --> 00:35:41.140
Excellent.
Kajiki, let us go to the temple.

00:35:54.070 --> 00:35:57.070
We are ready now.

00:35:57.280 --> 00:36:00.910
Mr. Shigure,
all of the crates have been secured.

00:36:01.030 --> 00:36:03.280
I see. Well done.

00:36:05.750 --> 00:36:06.910
Assemble!

00:36:12.170 --> 00:36:13.790
I thank you all.

00:36:13.920 --> 00:36:17.550
Our preparation is complete,
now we take action.

00:36:17.670 --> 00:36:21.300
Each of you has someone to whom
you must bid farewell.

00:36:22.390 --> 00:36:25.560
Tomorrow!
Finish all your farewells by tomorrow.

00:36:30.060 --> 00:36:31.480
You are still awake?

00:36:31.600 --> 00:36:32.860
Yes.

00:36:34.610 --> 00:36:36.820
Would you like some dinner?

00:36:38.780 --> 00:36:42.990
Toki, would you join me for dinner?

00:36:50.960 --> 00:36:53.420
I am going to leave on a long journey.

00:36:54.670 --> 00:36:56.670
I will go to Kyoto and then Aizu.

00:36:56.840 --> 00:36:57.670
I will go with you!

00:36:57.840 --> 00:37:01.680
No, you must stay here
and take care of our home.

00:37:01.840 --> 00:37:03.800
- But...
- I will write to you.

00:37:06.310 --> 00:37:08.680
Delicious.
May I have another bowl?

00:37:08.810 --> 00:37:09.770
Yes.

00:37:12.730 --> 00:37:16.230
It will be a long time before I eat
another of your homemade meals.

00:37:29.200 --> 00:37:30.160
What's up?

00:37:30.700 --> 00:37:33.460
They've met frequently
in the last few days.

00:37:33.580 --> 00:37:36.170
I see.
They may be taking action soon.

00:37:41.130 --> 00:37:43.260
See you tomorrow.

00:37:44.010 --> 00:37:45.720
Oh, Yahiko?

00:37:46.390 --> 00:37:47.470
Yes?

00:37:48.220 --> 00:37:50.930
You must grow up
to become a respectable man.

00:37:58.070 --> 00:37:59.320
Snow!

00:38:01.940 --> 00:38:04.070
We will now pray for
our client's continued success!

00:38:04.240 --> 00:38:05.950
Tori no Ichi...

00:38:06.070 --> 00:38:07.160
I am sorry I'm late.

00:38:07.280 --> 00:38:08.580
It's no problem.

00:38:09.080 --> 00:38:12.620
This is good.
I was hoping to see you again.

00:38:13.160 --> 00:38:17.960
Miss Toki is worried about you.

00:38:18.090 --> 00:38:21.630
I'm wondering what's on your mind,
Mr. Shigure?

00:38:22.420 --> 00:38:25.630
If something happens to me,
take care of Toki.

00:38:27.340 --> 00:38:29.560
There's a fight!

00:38:37.020 --> 00:38:39.820
Did you learn anything about Shigure?

00:38:39.940 --> 00:38:42.860
Yes, he's a very dangerous man.

00:38:42.990 --> 00:38:44.610
What do you mean by that?

00:38:45.400 --> 00:38:48.780
Shigure is drawing people to him.

00:38:50.410 --> 00:38:53.080
Survivors of the Shogitai.

00:38:55.210 --> 00:38:57.790
Survivors of the Battle of Aizu.

00:38:57.960 --> 00:39:00.210
Survivors of the Battle of Hakodate.

00:39:00.340 --> 00:39:03.960
All are people who have a grievance
with the current government.

00:39:07.840 --> 00:39:08.890
Why him?

00:39:09.010 --> 00:39:10.390
He's popular, I guess.

00:39:10.510 --> 00:39:11.810
Popular?

00:39:12.430 --> 00:39:15.020
They say he visits
the families of the men who died

00:39:15.140 --> 00:39:17.980
during the last battles
against the Shogunate.

00:39:18.150 --> 00:39:20.150
He comforts them as well.

00:39:20.270 --> 00:39:24.110
And his comforting includes
taking care of their financial problems.

00:39:24.230 --> 00:39:27.780
The rumor is that
he is planning a rebellion.

00:39:27.900 --> 00:39:31.660
Some say it is his path to atonement.

00:39:31.830 --> 00:39:33.290
Atonement, I see.

00:39:33.660 --> 00:39:36.080
The greatest threat is not Shigure.

00:39:36.200 --> 00:39:39.290
It is the men who surround him.

00:39:46.550 --> 00:39:49.890
<i>Yahiko, you must grow up</i>
<i>to become a respectable man.</i>

00:39:50.590 --> 00:39:54.010
Respectable man? What did he mean?

00:39:56.060 --> 00:39:57.230
Respectable?

00:39:57.350 --> 00:39:58.230
What?

00:39:58.350 --> 00:39:59.810
Man?

00:40:00.150 --> 00:40:02.230
He wasn't talking about those two!

00:40:05.530 --> 00:40:07.190
Mr. Musashino?

00:40:08.360 --> 00:40:09.410
What's going on?

00:40:25.750 --> 00:40:28.720
Finally, the time has come
for us to stand up!

00:40:28.880 --> 00:40:31.590
Our desires are ready to be realized!

00:40:31.720 --> 00:40:34.010
We have been branded as rebels,

00:40:34.140 --> 00:40:36.390
lost our comrades,
been covered with disgrace.

00:40:36.520 --> 00:40:39.060
We have been treated as enemies
by this new government!

00:40:43.900 --> 00:40:46.230
So as Aizu clan! So as Shogitai!

00:40:55.200 --> 00:40:56.830
Sanosuke!

00:40:58.160 --> 00:40:59.540
Kenshin...

00:40:59.660 --> 00:41:00.790
Why are you here?

00:41:00.910 --> 00:41:04.210
I heard some disturbing rumors
about Shigure.

00:41:04.330 --> 00:41:06.250
I came to discover the truth for myself.

00:41:06.380 --> 00:41:10.260
Rich businessmen with political influence
bribe the Meiji every day.

00:41:10.420 --> 00:41:13.260
The government is totally rotten!

00:41:14.140 --> 00:41:17.100
Remember what our late friend
Gentatsu Takatsuki once said,

00:41:17.260 --> 00:41:20.230
"The sky must be immeasurably
high and clear!"

00:41:20.350 --> 00:41:22.980
And, "All men must be equal
under the blue sky!"

00:41:23.100 --> 00:41:24.770
We must create that world!

00:41:26.270 --> 00:41:27.900
We will raise an army.

00:41:28.020 --> 00:41:30.240
The discontented will come to us
from all over Japan!

00:41:30.360 --> 00:41:35.700
We will start another Restoration!
The New Restoration!

00:41:37.160 --> 00:41:38.450
Who's there?!

00:41:41.200 --> 00:41:44.920
Bastard, how much did you hear?

00:41:45.040 --> 00:41:47.130
We cannot allow you to live now.

00:41:47.250 --> 00:41:48.550
- Yahiko?
- You will die!

00:41:48.670 --> 00:41:49.630
Wait!

00:41:49.800 --> 00:41:52.630
Mr. Shigure, let me join you.

00:41:52.800 --> 00:41:53.630
What?

00:41:53.800 --> 00:41:55.220
Please!

00:41:55.510 --> 00:41:59.100
Please give me a chance
to avenge my father's death.

00:41:59.220 --> 00:42:00.310
Please let me!

00:42:00.430 --> 00:42:01.640
Yahiko...

00:42:02.350 --> 00:42:05.310
Mr. Shigure, please accept him.
I ask you for this favor.

00:42:05.440 --> 00:42:06.480
Mr. Musashino!

00:42:08.190 --> 00:42:11.990
Survivors of the Battle of Aizu?
The Shogitai?

00:42:12.400 --> 00:42:15.160
- Yes, there seem to be a lot of them.
- Not good.

00:42:15.320 --> 00:42:16.780
Hey, Kenshin!

00:42:18.870 --> 00:42:19.830
Mr. Himura!

00:42:20.120 --> 00:42:21.790
Mr. Himura, do you know...

00:42:21.910 --> 00:42:23.660
Do you know where Shigure is?

00:42:23.830 --> 00:42:25.330
He's not home?

00:42:25.750 --> 00:42:28.210
I wish I had found this sooner.

00:42:28.340 --> 00:42:30.340
It was hidden behind
Gentatsu's memorial altar.

00:42:30.500 --> 00:42:32.170
May I see it?

00:42:32.510 --> 00:42:33.760
Yes.

00:42:35.760 --> 00:42:38.300
<i>The time has come for me</i>
<i>to keep my promise to Gentatsu.</i>

00:42:38.430 --> 00:42:40.640
<i>Farewell, I hope you have</i>
<i>a happier future.</i>

00:42:40.760 --> 00:42:43.930
<i>If you need any help,</i>
<i>please contact Mr. Himura.</i>

00:42:44.390 --> 00:42:45.690
Hey, this is a...

00:42:45.850 --> 00:42:47.440
What are you doing here?

00:42:47.810 --> 00:42:50.690
Miss Kaoru, where is Yahiko?

00:42:52.530 --> 00:42:56.950
Yahiko isn't at home,
so I assumed he was here.

00:42:57.530 --> 00:43:02.540
If we're going to find Yahiko,
we better find Shigure.

00:43:10.040 --> 00:43:11.710
They are on the move.

00:43:12.710 --> 00:43:13.920
But...

00:43:16.130 --> 00:43:18.390
What is their destination?

00:43:40.990 --> 00:43:43.410
The advance party is in place.

00:43:43.580 --> 00:43:46.000
I wish you all good luck
on your portion of the event.

00:43:46.410 --> 00:43:47.370
Yahiko?

00:43:48.040 --> 00:43:49.210
Yes, sir.

00:43:50.210 --> 00:43:51.590
What can I do for you?

00:43:51.750 --> 00:43:55.590
Yahiko,
I am impressed with your spirit.

00:43:55.760 --> 00:43:57.630
Thank you very much, sir.

00:43:58.430 --> 00:43:59.720
However...

00:44:06.810 --> 00:44:08.350
Mr. Shigure!

00:44:08.480 --> 00:44:10.350
Yahiko is just a child.

00:44:10.480 --> 00:44:12.400
If something were to happen to him,

00:44:12.520 --> 00:44:15.530
I do not know how
I would ever be able to face Mr. Himura.

00:44:16.030 --> 00:44:18.030
Mr. Shigure...

00:44:21.450 --> 00:44:22.780
I am sorry, Yahiko.

00:44:23.780 --> 00:44:25.450
I will go on ahead,
and make the final preparations.

00:44:25.580 --> 00:44:27.410
Of course, go. We must go too.

00:44:27.540 --> 00:44:28.540
Yes, sir.

00:44:59.530 --> 00:45:01.740
You're late, Kajiki.

00:45:05.290 --> 00:45:09.040
Pardon my lateness,
but our preparations are complete now.

00:45:09.160 --> 00:45:13.040
This removal of weapons from
the army arsenal was hard to conceal.

00:45:14.000 --> 00:45:15.340
Thank you.

00:45:15.460 --> 00:45:18.970
Here is a map of the parade route
with the guard postings marked.

00:45:19.090 --> 00:45:20.260
What about Shigure?

00:45:20.380 --> 00:45:23.390
He has no suspicions.

00:45:24.100 --> 00:45:25.640
He'll remain ignorant until the end.

00:45:25.810 --> 00:45:26.770
Yes, sir.

00:45:26.970 --> 00:45:29.230
Did you find out his view
on the points of attack?

00:45:29.350 --> 00:45:30.310
Yes, sir.

00:45:30.440 --> 00:45:33.980
He refuses to risk the lives
of any civilians during the attack.

00:45:34.310 --> 00:45:37.650
A person who believes such things
and tries to remain pure

00:45:37.820 --> 00:45:39.820
has no place in this world.

00:45:39.990 --> 00:45:43.320
I don't really care anyway.
I will take care of the guards.

00:45:43.450 --> 00:45:44.950
I appreciate that.

00:45:45.080 --> 00:45:49.410
And I managed to get Yamagata
to take the command for the day.

00:45:49.540 --> 00:45:52.290
The death of a foreign minister
in a place like this...

00:45:52.580 --> 00:45:55.380
Killed by
the army's own weaponry no less!

00:45:55.500 --> 00:45:57.500
Yamagata will be
thrown down from his position.

00:45:57.630 --> 00:46:00.380
And the next minister will be...

00:46:00.510 --> 00:46:02.300
You, Baron Tamono.

00:46:03.340 --> 00:46:08.350
The old man will be removed
and my time will finally come.

00:46:10.560 --> 00:46:13.230
Just make sure
that English bastard is killed!

00:46:13.850 --> 00:46:15.980
Yes, Baron Tamono.

00:46:16.110 --> 00:46:19.230
And when everything is done,
I will be...

00:46:19.480 --> 00:46:22.030
You will be rewarded
with a high government position.

00:46:22.200 --> 00:46:24.110
I want to ride
the winning horse this time.

00:46:24.240 --> 00:46:25.780
Trust me.

00:46:40.550 --> 00:46:44.930
Where in the hell is he?
We walked around all night.

00:46:45.050 --> 00:46:47.010
We looked everywhere
and turned up nothing.

00:46:47.890 --> 00:46:49.720
Are you feeling okay, Miss Toki?

00:46:49.850 --> 00:46:50.930
Yes.

00:46:51.560 --> 00:46:52.730
Yahiko...

00:46:53.560 --> 00:46:55.020
Miss Toki!

00:46:57.610 --> 00:46:59.070
Yahiko!

00:46:59.480 --> 00:47:00.690
Yahiko?

00:47:01.280 --> 00:47:02.570
Yahiko!

00:47:02.900 --> 00:47:05.910
You brat, where have you been?

00:47:06.070 --> 00:47:09.240
We've been worried about you.

00:47:15.620 --> 00:47:16.920
What?

00:47:18.460 --> 00:47:20.420
How dare you be so selfish?!

00:47:25.630 --> 00:47:31.640
I've really been worried sick about you.
We looked all over for you.

00:47:31.770 --> 00:47:34.350
I was going out of
my mind worrying that you died.

00:47:34.480 --> 00:47:35.770
Yahiko,

00:47:37.440 --> 00:47:38.770
I'm so relieved
to see that you're alive.

00:47:38.980 --> 00:47:43.400
If she hadn't slapped you,
I would have been glad to do it.

00:47:43.530 --> 00:47:45.780
I would have too, Yahiko.

00:47:46.400 --> 00:47:48.200
I'm so sorry.

00:47:48.320 --> 00:47:50.120
Where is Shigure?

00:47:50.280 --> 00:47:51.290
I don't know.

00:47:52.790 --> 00:47:55.750
This is very important.
Where did he go?

00:47:55.870 --> 00:47:58.580
I really don't know.
They left me behind.

00:47:58.880 --> 00:48:02.960
Come on, Yahiko, didn't you hear
them talking about anything?

00:48:03.130 --> 00:48:04.300
I'm telling you...

00:48:04.420 --> 00:48:05.670
Please!

00:48:05.970 --> 00:48:10.140
Please tell us what you know.
Anything you know!

00:48:10.260 --> 00:48:16.100
Just as Yahiko is important to Miss Kaoru
and Mr. Himura, Shigure is...

00:48:16.230 --> 00:48:20.270
Shigure is
the most important person to me!

00:48:20.400 --> 00:48:22.770
Please, Yahiko!

00:48:22.900 --> 00:48:25.690
Yahiko, don't you remember anything?

00:48:26.490 --> 00:48:28.030
Yahiko?

00:48:29.110 --> 00:48:30.620
They talked about
a guest of the nation or something.

00:48:30.740 --> 00:48:31.830
A guest of the nation?

00:48:31.950 --> 00:48:36.790
The British foreign minister
is coming to Tokyo, isn't he? Today!

00:48:37.330 --> 00:48:40.830
Yes, I read that there was going to
be a parade in his honor.

00:48:41.500 --> 00:48:43.380
A guest of the nation...

00:48:43.500 --> 00:48:46.340
Mr. Himura, please stop Shigure!

00:48:47.420 --> 00:48:51.510
Please! Please!

00:48:52.300 --> 00:48:54.060
Please...

00:49:20.040 --> 00:49:22.710
What a grand parade.

00:49:23.290 --> 00:49:27.880
This is the first time
a foreign minister has visited Tokyo.

00:49:28.050 --> 00:49:30.880
All the more reason
this day must end safely.

00:49:41.690 --> 00:49:44.360
If they are planning anything,
this will surely be their target.

00:49:44.480 --> 00:49:45.440
Yes, sir.

00:49:55.070 --> 00:49:58.450
Minister, it looks like
all has been successful.

00:49:58.580 --> 00:49:59.620
Yes.

00:50:03.460 --> 00:50:06.960
<i>Enjoy your final moments</i>
<i>as Minister of the Army.</i>

00:50:07.090 --> 00:50:11.130
<i>I will take advantage of your relaxation,</i>
<i>thinking everything is over.</i>

00:50:17.260 --> 00:50:18.140
Ready.

00:50:45.920 --> 00:50:46.790
Hurry up!

00:50:46.960 --> 00:50:48.630
Protect the foreign minister!

00:50:51.550 --> 00:50:52.550
Look at that smoke!

00:50:52.670 --> 00:50:54.430
It's from the guesthouse!

00:51:04.640 --> 00:51:05.980
Let's go!

00:51:13.280 --> 00:51:14.610
Charge!

00:51:32.010 --> 00:51:33.380
Get out of my way!

00:51:35.590 --> 00:51:38.140
I declare the beginning of
the New Restoration!

00:51:38.470 --> 00:51:42.060
Shigure! Shigure! Shigure!

00:51:54.900 --> 00:51:56.570
Kill each other for all I care.

00:52:09.880 --> 00:52:11.130
I need another round!

00:52:11.250 --> 00:52:12.670
You won't need it.

00:52:24.720 --> 00:52:26.180
What happened to the foreign minister?

00:52:27.690 --> 00:52:29.600
I found the foreign minister!

00:52:38.780 --> 00:52:40.570
You must die!

00:52:44.870 --> 00:52:46.000
What?!

00:52:51.880 --> 00:52:53.590
Stop this at once.

00:52:53.710 --> 00:52:54.800
Don't interfere!

00:52:54.920 --> 00:52:56.760
Withdraw your men!

00:52:56.920 --> 00:52:58.130
Get out of my way, Himura!

00:52:58.260 --> 00:53:00.590
I will not.

00:53:00.720 --> 00:53:02.050
Then I will kill you first!

00:53:06.930 --> 00:53:08.310
The reversed blade sword...

00:53:08.430 --> 00:53:11.270
I wanted to avoid
fighting you most of all.

00:53:12.110 --> 00:53:14.270
As did I.

00:53:14.570 --> 00:53:17.570
That is irrelevant now!

00:53:31.080 --> 00:53:32.290
Stop this!

00:53:36.000 --> 00:53:38.970
You don't gain anything
with this foolishness!

00:53:39.130 --> 00:53:41.090
Use your brains!

00:54:24.590 --> 00:54:26.510
Gentatsu! Where is Gentatsu?

00:54:34.150 --> 00:54:36.020
Gentatsu!

00:54:47.830 --> 00:54:50.500
Gentatsu!

00:54:54.460 --> 00:54:56.210
That was you!

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:02.380
Saiki Kanuma Swordsmanship!

00:55:02.510 --> 00:55:03.930
I will never forgive you!

00:55:10.970 --> 00:55:12.310
Take the foreign minister
into the guesthouse immediately.

00:55:12.430 --> 00:55:13.850
Quickly!

00:55:13.980 --> 00:55:15.480
Fire! Fire!

00:55:45.550 --> 00:55:46.720
Musashino!

00:55:46.840 --> 00:55:49.350
Mr. Shigure...

00:55:49.930 --> 00:55:52.470
Please...

00:55:52.810 --> 00:55:54.390
Musashino!

00:55:56.560 --> 00:55:57.940
Hurry!

00:56:00.400 --> 00:56:02.730
Protect the perimeter!
Don't let them escape!

00:56:03.690 --> 00:56:05.610
Mr. Shigure, please hurry.

00:56:07.570 --> 00:56:10.490
I will settle this one day, at any cost.

00:56:31.720 --> 00:56:33.390
What in the world?

00:56:39.560 --> 00:56:40.480
Yahiko?

00:56:55.160 --> 00:56:57.080
Mr. Musashino...

00:56:57.460 --> 00:56:59.080
Mr. Musashino!

00:56:59.210 --> 00:57:01.710
Mr. Musashino! Mr. Musashino!

00:57:01.830 --> 00:57:03.630
Mr. Musashino!

00:57:06.050 --> 00:57:07.760
This can't be!

00:57:10.340 --> 00:57:13.510
Mr. Musashino! Mr. Musashino!

00:58:16.700 --> 00:58:22.540
Hitokiri Gentatsu, we fought
all those years ago for one reason.

00:58:25.250 --> 00:58:28.130
We wanted to make sure that
no such battles ever took place again.

00:58:28.840 --> 00:58:32.720
I never wanted to feel this sadness again.

00:58:34.090 --> 00:58:35.550
Kenshin...

00:58:51.650 --> 00:58:53.400
Gentatsu,

00:58:55.110 --> 00:58:59.450
I will do everything
in my power to stop that man.

00:59:09.130 --> 00:59:11.130
What's going on?

00:59:12.920 --> 00:59:16.090
Minister, these cannons belong to
the army, don't they?

00:59:16.220 --> 00:59:17.180
Yes.

00:59:17.300 --> 00:59:20.510
Why does the rebel army
have our cannons?

00:59:21.640 --> 00:59:23.520
Damn, those idiots failed.

00:59:27.350 --> 00:59:30.270
The rebel army has barricaded themselves
in the forest of Ueno.

00:59:30.400 --> 00:59:31.320
What did you say?

00:59:31.440 --> 00:59:35.070
Ueno? They are acting just
like the Shogitai, aren't they?

00:59:35.610 --> 00:59:38.320
They are surrounded and
under constant surveillance.

00:59:38.450 --> 00:59:39.910
Minister!

00:59:40.410 --> 00:59:45.620
Sir, I can finish them off.

00:59:46.790 --> 00:59:47.880
Well, then.

00:59:48.790 --> 00:59:50.630
Wait a moment.

00:59:50.750 --> 00:59:55.050
Just who are you?
Do you know who I am?

00:59:55.170 --> 00:59:57.840
I am Baron Tamono of the Imperial Guard,

00:59:57.970 --> 01:00:00.970
and that is Army Minister Yamagata.

01:00:02.430 --> 01:00:05.520
Tamono, let him approach.

01:00:09.310 --> 01:00:10.690
Mr. Yamagata.

01:00:10.820 --> 01:00:13.480
Himura, as you can see,
we are in a very critical situation.

01:00:13.610 --> 01:00:15.820
If this is not an emergency,
please let it wait until later.

01:00:15.950 --> 01:00:17.910
You must hold off your attack.

01:00:18.030 --> 01:00:19.070
What?

01:00:19.200 --> 01:00:23.330
I know the rebel leader.

01:00:24.700 --> 01:00:27.870
You're not saying
you want to go in there alone, are you?

01:00:29.210 --> 01:00:30.540
That is utterly careless!

01:00:30.670 --> 01:00:32.340
It shames me to say this,

01:00:32.460 --> 01:00:35.710
but the rebels used
army weaponry for their attack.

01:00:36.170 --> 01:00:38.260
The roots of this incident run very deep.

01:00:38.630 --> 01:00:42.140
Himura, that man is
the cause of this carnage.

01:00:42.260 --> 01:00:44.350
We can't wait for long.

01:00:44.810 --> 01:00:46.640
That is fine.

01:00:49.900 --> 01:00:51.610
You are not asking me to wait,
are you?

01:00:51.730 --> 01:00:54.860
Minister, you must order me
to launch a full attack!

01:00:54.980 --> 01:00:57.070
We will place our faith
in Himura for now.

01:00:57.400 --> 01:01:02.830
If anyone can end this bloodlessly,
it will be him.

01:01:02.950 --> 01:01:04.580
<i>I trust you, Himura.</i>

01:01:06.620 --> 01:01:08.250
Miss Toki, please wait!

01:01:09.160 --> 01:01:10.710
Miss Toki, calm down.

01:01:10.830 --> 01:01:13.920
I have to go with Shigure.

01:01:14.750 --> 01:01:16.300
Mr. Himura!

01:01:18.260 --> 01:01:22.220
Shigure... Shigure plans to die!

01:01:22.850 --> 01:01:27.600
He has always blamed himself
for my brother's death.

01:01:27.770 --> 01:01:29.230
If he dies...

01:01:31.600 --> 01:01:35.730
Miss Toki, I promise
I will bring Mr. Shigure back to you.

01:01:37.280 --> 01:01:41.950
Don't worry.
Kenshin will help you, okay?

01:01:42.360 --> 01:01:44.120
Oh, Miss Kaoru!

01:01:47.080 --> 01:01:48.160
Kenshin?

01:01:52.120 --> 01:01:54.790
Kenshin,
will you go in there alone?

01:01:55.130 --> 01:01:56.130
But...

01:01:56.250 --> 01:02:00.220
Miss Toki's brother was killed
during the Bakumatsu.

01:02:00.340 --> 01:02:01.340
She told me that.

01:02:01.470 --> 01:02:04.390
The man who killed him was...

01:02:05.350 --> 01:02:07.100
The Hitokiri Battosai.

01:02:09.680 --> 01:02:11.100
It was me.

01:02:12.520 --> 01:02:13.810
Oh, no.

01:02:14.310 --> 01:02:18.440
That is the main reason
Shigure caused this travesty.

01:02:18.570 --> 01:02:22.320
Therefore, I have to take
responsibility for it as well.

01:02:23.200 --> 01:02:24.820
Oh, no...

01:02:26.280 --> 01:02:27.790
No!

01:02:46.850 --> 01:02:49.680
Kenshin...

01:02:57.900 --> 01:02:59.030
Hurry up!

01:02:59.110 --> 01:03:00.950
This barricade must be
built on the double!

01:03:01.110 --> 01:03:04.240
If we don't hurry,
the government forces will break in!

01:03:04.370 --> 01:03:07.620
<i>Damn! Why should</i>
<i>we lock ourselves in this place?</i>

01:03:07.790 --> 01:03:10.920
<i>Does Shigure want to be</i>
<i>just like the Shogitai?</i>

01:03:13.920 --> 01:03:15.130
<i>I don't care.</i>

01:03:15.250 --> 01:03:19.720
<i>When push comes to shove,</i>
<i>I'll slip over to Tamono's side.</i>

01:03:19.840 --> 01:03:23.970
<i>I have too much information</i>
<i>on Tamono's dealings.</i>

01:03:24.090 --> 01:03:26.640
<i>He would never betray me.</i>

01:03:39.150 --> 01:03:40.990
You're late, Kenshin.

01:03:41.110 --> 01:03:44.410
They've cornered themselves
behind those barricades.

01:03:44.820 --> 01:03:48.330
Now that they've settled in,
they don't seem to want to move at all.

01:03:48.450 --> 01:03:52.410
I wonder if Shigure is laying in
wait for you, Kenshin?

01:03:53.830 --> 01:03:55.040
Tamono?

01:03:56.040 --> 01:03:56.960
Let them through.

01:03:57.090 --> 01:03:58.090
Yes, sir!

01:04:05.680 --> 01:04:07.470
I wonder if we'll ever see you again?

01:04:07.890 --> 01:04:10.810
That guy is such a jerk.

01:04:21.530 --> 01:04:22.900
Someone's coming!

01:04:23.400 --> 01:04:25.070
- What?!
- A soldier?

01:04:30.490 --> 01:04:32.710
Let me handle this.

01:04:32.830 --> 01:04:34.370
It's very dangerous up there,
so move it.

01:04:34.620 --> 01:04:35.960
What do you mean?

01:04:45.130 --> 01:04:46.010
Hey!

01:04:47.050 --> 01:04:48.680
I told you it was dangerous.

01:04:56.190 --> 01:04:59.060
Kenshin, they're just children.

01:05:02.690 --> 01:05:05.360
Hey, what are you doing?

01:05:05.490 --> 01:05:08.870
These are government spies!
Kill them! Kill them both!

01:05:11.120 --> 01:05:15.370
I don't want to,
but I'll take care of this, Kenshin.

01:05:15.500 --> 01:05:17.210
Thank you, Sano.

01:05:18.420 --> 01:05:20.790
Yeah, you can count on me.

01:05:21.880 --> 01:05:24.590
All right, kids! Let's go!

01:05:24.720 --> 01:05:26.470
I'm going to teach you how to fight!

01:05:27.130 --> 01:05:28.760
Your leg position is too open.

01:05:28.930 --> 01:05:30.550
You leave your jaw too exposed.

01:05:32.100 --> 01:05:34.520
Don't play with a sword like toy!

01:05:34.930 --> 01:05:36.730
Kenshin, hurry up!

01:05:42.070 --> 01:05:44.070
I can't fight rifles
at this short range.

01:05:44.280 --> 01:05:47.320
Very good! Now finish them off!

01:05:47.450 --> 01:05:48.950
Leave them alone.

01:05:50.410 --> 01:05:52.280
Shigure?

01:05:53.580 --> 01:05:55.500
He came to see me.

01:05:59.790 --> 01:06:01.960
Kenshin, I'll leave this one to you.

01:06:02.090 --> 01:06:06.010
Back up, everybody!
This is going to be dangerous. You too!

01:06:06.130 --> 01:06:08.680
I knew you would come.

01:06:09.300 --> 01:06:11.760
We must settle this now.

01:06:13.850 --> 01:06:17.140
I have something to tell you.

01:06:17.310 --> 01:06:19.350
The one who killed Gentatsu...

01:06:19.650 --> 01:06:21.980
It was you, Hitokiri Battosai!

01:06:24.150 --> 01:06:26.400
I realized it during our last fight.

01:06:28.280 --> 01:06:29.990
If your anger towards me
has caused you to do this...

01:06:30.110 --> 01:06:33.200
No, Gentatsu risked his life
when he fought you,

01:06:33.330 --> 01:06:35.790
and you risked yours.

01:06:35.910 --> 01:06:37.870
In a duel, death is no one's fault.

01:06:40.370 --> 01:06:41.830
However, Himura,

01:06:42.000 --> 01:06:44.290
look at the hell society is living in
because of the Meiji government.

01:06:44.420 --> 01:06:46.760
We all risked our lives back then.

01:06:46.880 --> 01:06:49.300
I risked mine along with you and Gentatsu.

01:06:49.420 --> 01:06:51.510
But now that the victors have control,

01:06:51.680 --> 01:06:54.680
they demand to be honored,
use their power unwisely,

01:06:54.810 --> 01:06:56.270
and do nothing but covet money.

01:06:56.930 --> 01:07:00.810
They have disgraced the memories
of those like Gentatsu

01:07:00.940 --> 01:07:03.190
who fought from pure motives.

01:07:03.360 --> 01:07:06.900
Can you forgive a government
that acts in such a manner?

01:07:07.490 --> 01:07:08.360
I...

01:07:08.530 --> 01:07:12.030
Did you kill so many men
in the service of a system like that?

01:07:16.870 --> 01:07:22.880
If you did, the people killed by
your sword will rest uneasily,

01:07:23.040 --> 01:07:25.210
Hitokiri Battosai.

01:07:26.040 --> 01:07:30.590
Himura, we will start
a New Restoration.

01:07:31.220 --> 01:07:36.640
Once again, we will define good and
sort out the evil in our midst.

01:07:38.560 --> 01:07:42.310
That is the only way to serve
the memories of those who died.

01:07:42.440 --> 01:07:47.230
To honor those who died so young.

01:07:47.400 --> 01:07:52.200
Do you want to atone for their loss
by shedding more blood of young men?

01:07:55.370 --> 01:07:59.910
Do you want to make a new world
by trampling over more bodies?

01:08:00.040 --> 01:08:02.160
By making more people bleed?!

01:08:08.300 --> 01:08:12.260
That is the greatest betrayal of those
who died in the war.

01:08:12.420 --> 01:08:14.590
It is your betrayal.

01:08:18.760 --> 01:08:22.390
I am a former Aizu samurai.
I use Saiki Kanuma technique.

01:08:22.520 --> 01:08:25.190
I am Takimi Shigure.

01:08:25.310 --> 01:08:26.440
Ready!

01:08:26.610 --> 01:08:29.270
I use Hiten Mitsurugi technique.
I am Kenshin Himura.

01:08:33.900 --> 01:08:35.450
Kenshin...

01:08:40.580 --> 01:08:42.450
<i>During the Bakumatsu,</i>

01:08:42.580 --> 01:08:44.830
<i>Saiki Kanuma technique was</i>
<i>used for indoor fights.</i>

01:08:44.960 --> 01:08:48.710
<i>How will it work here?</i>
<i>How will he attack?</i>

01:08:51.550 --> 01:08:53.720
Kanuma Erasing Moon Slash.

01:09:01.810 --> 01:09:05.640
<i>Don't let the sheath distract you.</i>
<i>Will he attack from the left?</i>

01:09:05.770 --> 01:09:09.940
<i>Or the right?</i>
<i>Or from above? Or below?</i>

01:09:25.750 --> 01:09:27.000
Kenshin...

01:09:30.670 --> 01:09:31.840
He's coming.

01:09:37.090 --> 01:09:38.470
From below!

01:09:43.680 --> 01:09:47.640
Hiten Mitsurugi Dragon's Hammer Flash!

01:09:52.690 --> 01:09:57.360
I predicted your sword's movement.
The line of your attack.

01:09:57.950 --> 01:09:59.780
I will never forget it.

01:10:07.210 --> 01:10:11.080
Hiten Mitsurugi Flying Dragon Flash!

01:10:13.840 --> 01:10:17.130
A swift stroke and then a pause.
I know it all too well.

01:10:17.260 --> 01:10:20.470
It was seared into my memory and
has haunted me for fourteen years.

01:10:24.060 --> 01:10:26.810
Kanuma Erasing Sun Slash!

01:10:28.390 --> 01:10:30.480
Iron sheath!

01:10:33.230 --> 01:10:34.940
Kenshin!

01:10:38.570 --> 01:10:40.320
Erasing Sun Slash!

01:10:40.570 --> 01:10:43.990
<i>I see, a double attack</i>
<i>within a circle. But...</i>

01:10:56.960 --> 01:10:58.760
I am better than Gentatsu.

01:11:01.550 --> 01:11:02.850
<i>Kenshin!</i>

01:11:10.770 --> 01:11:13.190
Everything will be all right.
Kenshin can handle this situation.

01:11:13.310 --> 01:11:15.440
Mr. Shigure will be all right.

01:11:15.610 --> 01:11:17.110
Right, Miss Toki?

01:11:17.940 --> 01:11:19.570
Miss Toki?!

01:11:26.540 --> 01:11:29.580
<i>I can barely move my arm.</i>

01:11:29.710 --> 01:11:30.830
Himura,

01:11:32.120 --> 01:11:37.670
if you do not use the blade of your sword,
you will die tonight.

01:11:44.680 --> 01:11:46.810
Now, turn your sword over.

01:11:49.640 --> 01:11:54.940
I don't mind shedding my own blood,
no matter how much blood flows.

01:12:01.030 --> 01:12:05.660
However,
I won't let you make others bleed!

01:12:06.410 --> 01:12:09.410
Then you will die here!

01:12:18.460 --> 01:12:23.630
<i>I only need one attack, just one.</i>

01:12:24.340 --> 01:12:26.220
His posture is of
Hiten Mitsurugi's ultimate technique,

01:12:26.340 --> 01:12:27.890
Flying Sky Dragon Flash.

01:12:29.140 --> 01:12:32.060
Kanuma Erasing Flame Slash!

01:12:36.020 --> 01:12:37.360
He flies?

01:12:40.190 --> 01:12:42.490
That's the same attack as before.

01:12:44.030 --> 01:12:45.860
It will be useless to you!

01:12:46.870 --> 01:12:47.740
That's not it.

01:12:47.870 --> 01:12:52.830
It's not the Dragon's Hammer Flash,
or the Flying Dragon Slash.

01:12:52.960 --> 01:12:54.290
What is it?

01:12:56.420 --> 01:12:59.210
There's no stable foothold in the air.

01:12:59.420 --> 01:13:02.090
Kanuma Double Head Slash!

01:13:11.140 --> 01:13:14.730
He used the force of his turning body
to draw his sword.

01:13:19.520 --> 01:13:22.030
Incredible. That was incredible.

01:13:22.690 --> 01:13:25.070
It's Kenshin's
original sword-drawing technique.

01:13:35.250 --> 01:13:38.250
Why didn't you cut me?

01:13:38.380 --> 01:13:41.000
In honor of the men I killed,

01:13:41.130 --> 01:13:43.630
I vowed to never use my sword
to kill anyone ever again.

01:13:44.260 --> 01:13:48.260
That's the only way
I can do to atone for them.

01:13:55.100 --> 01:13:56.690
Gentatsu...

01:13:58.270 --> 01:14:01.980
Shigure, I love the blue sky
over Mount Bandai.

01:14:04.480 --> 01:14:05.990
I do too.

01:14:08.490 --> 01:14:12.450
The blue sky must be high and clear
no matter how far away it is.

01:14:12.620 --> 01:14:13.450
Yes.

01:14:13.620 --> 01:14:17.210
The whole world should be like that.

01:14:21.960 --> 01:14:23.500
Gentatsu...

01:14:23.630 --> 01:14:27.470
For your sake, Gentatsu,

01:14:27.590 --> 01:14:30.550
I won't lose this battle.

01:14:41.020 --> 01:14:41.980
Let's go.

01:14:43.270 --> 01:14:44.770
Stop!

01:14:49.490 --> 01:14:52.700
Stop! Stop it!

01:14:57.290 --> 01:14:58.620
Toki?

01:14:58.750 --> 01:15:00.210
You...

01:15:01.670 --> 01:15:04.840
You have had enough.

01:15:04.960 --> 01:15:07.300
Please stop this now.

01:15:17.850 --> 01:15:19.020
Toki...

01:15:19.180 --> 01:15:20.810
Gentatsu...

01:15:23.560 --> 01:15:27.480
Would Gentatsu want to see
Miss Toki crying like this?

01:15:37.700 --> 01:15:40.120
What's the matter, Gentatsu?

01:15:40.370 --> 01:15:42.620
I can't sleep at night.

01:15:43.540 --> 01:15:47.090
The men I've killed have mothers
and fathers, sisters and brothers.

01:15:47.210 --> 01:15:50.130
They have people they love.

01:15:50.260 --> 01:15:53.220
I keep thinking about that.

01:15:54.090 --> 01:15:55.850
Gentatsu...

01:15:57.680 --> 01:15:59.560
I know.

01:15:59.720 --> 01:16:02.390
What did the letter
from your family say?

01:16:02.520 --> 01:16:05.310
My father has fallen ill again.

01:16:06.110 --> 01:16:09.780
His symptoms have returned,
but I can't worry about him.

01:16:09.900 --> 01:16:11.110
With the Choshu clan on the move...

01:16:11.240 --> 01:16:13.070
You're wrong, Shigure.

01:16:14.320 --> 01:16:19.330
Toki is all I have left.
That is probably why I feel this way.

01:16:19.450 --> 01:16:24.330
But you cannot be ashamed
of loving your family.

01:16:24.460 --> 01:16:26.080
If you do not love your family,

01:16:26.250 --> 01:16:28.920
you have no qualifications to care
about your country or the world.

01:16:29.050 --> 01:16:33.590
Do you know why I use my sword
despite being called Hitokiri?

01:16:33.760 --> 01:16:38.300
It is because of my friends,
your family, and for Toki.

01:16:38.430 --> 01:16:42.390
I want the people I love to be happy.

01:16:48.270 --> 01:16:49.860
Gentatsu...

01:17:02.790 --> 01:17:05.750
Gentatsu... Gentatsu!

01:17:05.870 --> 01:17:11.170
There is a man who
honors your death more than I.

01:17:14.800 --> 01:17:16.220
I...

01:17:18.850 --> 01:17:21.060
I have lost.

01:17:30.520 --> 01:17:32.980
The man behind the uprising
is Baron Tamono.

01:17:33.190 --> 01:17:35.110
What are you saying?

01:17:36.820 --> 01:17:38.990
This one confessed everything.

01:17:39.110 --> 01:17:40.030
Who is he?

01:17:40.160 --> 01:17:42.120
He works in the arms depot.

01:17:42.530 --> 01:17:47.540
The rebels used weapons that
were given to them by Tamono.

01:17:47.660 --> 01:17:49.460
My god!

01:17:49.580 --> 01:17:53.880
He also told us who
Tamono's contact in the rebel army is.

01:17:57.550 --> 01:18:00.390
I will report this
to the minister at once.

01:18:07.520 --> 01:18:09.020
Mr. Shigure!

01:18:09.140 --> 01:18:11.230
Are you okay, Mr. Shigure?

01:18:11.350 --> 01:18:14.020
I'm fine. Don't make such a fuss.

01:18:14.150 --> 01:18:15.900
Mr. Shigure! Mr. Shigure!

01:18:16.110 --> 01:18:18.400
Mr. Shigure! Mr. Shigure!

01:18:22.160 --> 01:18:24.410
Toki, please come here.

01:18:25.240 --> 01:18:26.500
Yes.

01:18:32.080 --> 01:18:34.380
Toki, I will turn myself
in to the authorities.

01:18:34.500 --> 01:18:35.420
Yes.

01:18:37.510 --> 01:18:42.760
Toki, I have been making you cry
all this time, haven't I?

01:18:51.100 --> 01:18:53.270
Will you survive with
that wound, Kenshin?

01:18:53.440 --> 01:18:54.770
Yes.

01:18:54.900 --> 01:18:57.900
Watching them, this wound...

01:18:58.360 --> 01:19:02.490
Forgot about the pain? You would.

01:19:15.210 --> 01:19:17.130
Aim well!

01:19:20.630 --> 01:19:22.550
Fire! Fire!

01:19:24.390 --> 01:19:26.350
What the hell is this?

01:19:57.090 --> 01:20:00.000
Is Kenshin still in there?

01:20:02.630 --> 01:20:03.630
Kenshin...

01:20:04.590 --> 01:20:06.340
Shigure! Shigure!

01:20:07.390 --> 01:20:08.890
Mr. Shigure!

01:20:09.760 --> 01:20:11.220
Mr. Shigure!

01:20:11.350 --> 01:20:12.810
Shigure!

01:20:15.690 --> 01:20:18.770
Toki, are you there?

01:20:19.020 --> 01:20:23.030
I am. I am right here.

01:20:24.400 --> 01:20:29.370
Gentatsu, the blue sky
has to be high and clear,

01:20:29.490 --> 01:20:33.040
no matter how far away it is.

01:20:34.710 --> 01:20:36.370
Shigure?

01:20:39.540 --> 01:20:42.130
Shigure!

01:20:51.970 --> 01:20:54.730
<i>The next volley will kill the rest of them.</i>

01:20:54.890 --> 01:20:59.560
<i>Who would have guessed that I would conspire</i>
<i>with Kajiki, the poor bastard?</i>

01:21:04.070 --> 01:21:05.650
Why?

01:21:06.070 --> 01:21:07.860
Why did you fire at them?!

01:21:08.530 --> 01:21:10.450
Idiot.

01:21:12.120 --> 01:21:15.250
You all are going to die now.

01:21:15.460 --> 01:21:18.000
You!

01:21:24.550 --> 01:21:27.550
Fire! Kill them all!

01:21:27.680 --> 01:21:30.930
Damn! Everyone hide behind something!
Anything!

01:21:31.100 --> 01:21:32.470
Kenshin!

01:21:36.230 --> 01:21:37.730
He's escaping! Shoot him!

01:21:46.280 --> 01:21:47.280
What?!

01:21:50.570 --> 01:21:52.370
What are you doing?
Hurry up and shoot him!

01:21:56.620 --> 01:21:57.500
Kenshin!

01:22:21.230 --> 01:22:22.310
Kenshin!

01:22:26.360 --> 01:22:28.320
Hold your fire!

01:22:28.950 --> 01:22:32.700
The battle is over.
Put your guns down!

01:22:39.660 --> 01:22:43.790
Remove the injured by stretcher.
Bring in medical supplies.

01:22:43.920 --> 01:22:45.000
Arrest Tamono!

01:22:45.130 --> 01:22:49.090
Listen, you guys,
you're lucky to be alive, aren't you?

01:22:57.520 --> 01:23:00.560
Damn it! Tamono has betrayed me.

01:23:00.690 --> 01:23:03.060
You are the traitor, though.

01:23:03.190 --> 01:23:05.690
You threw over your best friend
to gain influence with your enemy.

01:23:05.820 --> 01:23:09.650
You live your life by testing the wind
and going in its direction.

01:23:11.650 --> 01:23:14.370
I might be wrong.
Maybe you are just flexible.

01:23:14.570 --> 01:23:16.030
What did you say?!

01:23:16.160 --> 01:23:18.240
I am waiting.

01:23:18.370 --> 01:23:21.660
I chose the place you will die,
so draw your sword as you will.

01:23:21.960 --> 01:23:23.370
Wait a minute!

01:23:23.540 --> 01:23:28.000
I know everything that happened.
I can testify against Tamono.

01:23:28.130 --> 01:23:30.720
Why don't we make a deal?

01:23:32.340 --> 01:23:36.720
I will not be killed by a corrupt man
who stands for false justice!

01:23:39.140 --> 01:23:43.190
I forgot to tell you my definition of justice.

01:23:43.310 --> 01:23:45.730
It is to kill evil immediately.

01:23:47.060 --> 01:23:51.740
Shinsengumi, Hajime Saito...

01:24:05.750 --> 01:24:08.290
May we move him?

01:24:10.590 --> 01:24:15.300
A little longer. Let me stay
with him a little longer, please.

01:24:15.430 --> 01:24:16.390
Yes, Ma'am.

01:24:47.290 --> 01:24:48.790
Hello!

01:24:48.960 --> 01:24:50.000
Goodbye!

01:24:50.130 --> 01:24:51.300
Be careful out there.

01:24:51.460 --> 01:24:52.460
Yes, sir!

01:24:53.630 --> 01:24:55.090
Mr. Himura?

01:25:01.470 --> 01:25:03.100
What can I do for you?

01:25:03.220 --> 01:25:06.810
I must tell you something, Miss Toki.

01:25:08.980 --> 01:25:12.900
The man who killed Gentatsu was me.

01:25:13.940 --> 01:25:20.320
During the Bakumatsu,
I was known as the Hitokiri Battosai.

01:25:23.870 --> 01:25:25.830
Did Shigure know this?

01:25:32.090 --> 01:25:35.340
I see.

01:25:36.170 --> 01:25:40.260
Shigure told me that
the Bakumatsu was incredibly chaotic.

01:25:40.390 --> 01:25:45.560
Nobody could tell good from evil.

01:25:45.680 --> 01:25:52.690
He said that people fought solely
for what was in their hearts.

01:25:52.820 --> 01:25:56.940
I believe what he said.

01:26:03.830 --> 01:26:08.830
I am going to travel to Shigure's hometown
to bury his belongings.

01:26:08.960 --> 01:26:10.790
Thank you for everything.

01:26:10.920 --> 01:26:12.380
Take care, Miss Toki.

01:26:12.540 --> 01:26:13.840
I hope you come back soon.

01:26:13.960 --> 01:26:16.340
I will. The children will be waiting.

01:26:16.460 --> 01:26:17.840
At your private school?

01:26:18.010 --> 01:26:21.010
Yes, and someday I want to teach
this story to my students.

01:26:21.140 --> 01:26:25.220
They should know how people lived
and felt during the Bakumatsu.

01:26:25.350 --> 01:26:30.230
They might grow up to create the world
Shigure dreamed of.

01:26:30.390 --> 01:26:33.440
One in which no blood is shed.

01:26:33.560 --> 01:26:36.980
I hope that someday you will visit
my brother and Shigure's graves.

01:26:37.110 --> 01:26:39.950
I most definitely will.

01:26:40.070 --> 01:26:42.820
When the flowers are in bloom,
let's all visit his grave together.

01:26:42.950 --> 01:26:44.700
- Good idea!
- Yeah!

01:26:44.830 --> 01:26:46.370
Be careful!

01:27:00.840 --> 01:27:05.470
The blue sky should be high and clear
no matter how far away it is.

01:27:05.600 --> 01:27:07.930
Isn't that right?
